# Two kinds of flower {#sec:flowers}

A hazel carries its male and female flowers on the same branch, as
@fig:catkins shows. The image sits beside this book's file, which is why the
book is a folder (`catkins/book.hdoc`) rather than a single file.

![Male catkins and female flowers on the same branch in
February.](catkins.png){#fig:catkins}

# Counting flowers {#sec:counting}

A branch with $m$ male catkins and $f$ female flowers sets at most $f$ nuts.
The share of female flowers, @eq:share, is what a grower watches:

$$
s = \frac{f}{m + f}, \qquad 0 \le s \le 1
$$ {#eq:share}
